                                                        "score": 1,
                                                        "subjectMatched": "Lee Lawrence",
                                                        "text": "Man jailed for gun and drugs offences AN Old Trafford man has been jailed for seven years after officers found a gun, bullets and drugs under his bed. Lee Lawrence, 28, of Princess Court, had pleaded guilty at Minshull Street crown Court on Friday to possession of a firearm, possession of ammunition, possession of cocaine with intent to supply and possession of cannabis. He was sentenced to five years for the firearm and ammunition offences, to run concurrently, and two years for the drug offences, to run consecutively. Officers acting on intelligence executed a search warrant at a flat on Princess Court last November. During the subsequent search officers found a black shoulder bag under Lawrence's bed. It contained a handgun, 31 .22 bullets, a brass knuckle-duster with a folding knife, 62 snap bags containing cannabis and a plastic bag believed to contain cocaine. The gun had two bullets in its chamber and had no safety catch, meaning it was ready to be fired. Lawrence admitted it was his flat during formal interviews and said he knew about the bag and its contents. He claimed he was holding the gun and bullets for gang members who had approached him in the street and forced him to stash the items. Detective Constable Stu Brown, of Stretford CID, said: \"In recovering this gun, we undoubtedly stopped someone from being shot and possibly killed at some point. \"But what today shows is the dramatic strides we have taken towards removing guns from our streets and making them a much safer place to live \"In cases like this the information we receive from the public is crucial. I hope this sentence reassures and encourages members of the community who are worried about criminality in their area that if they do have information, it will be treated in the strictest of confidence, we can protect them and we will bring people like Lawrence to justice.\"",
